EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "Ragas Context Recall", url: "https://docs.ragas.io/en/stable/concepts/metrics/available_metrics/context_recall/", overlap: "Ships a RAG retrieval metric that breaks the reference answer into claims and measures whether claims are attributable to retrieved contexts; overlaps with answer-completeness as an answer-support/coverage metric, but not the exact fixed-chunk whole-gold-span containment diagnostic."},
  {system: "DeepEval ContextualRecallMetric", url: "https://deepeval.com/docs/metrics-contextual-recall", overlap: "Ships contextual recall for RAG by extracting statements from expected_output and classifying attribution to retrieval_context; close competitor to completeness@k and evidence that practitioners already evaluate whether retrieved context supports the expected answer."},
  {system: "LlamaIndex RetrieverEvaluator", url: "https://developers.llamaindex.ai/python/examples/evaluation/retrieval/retriever_eval/", overlap: "Ships standard retrieval metrics including hit-rate, MRR, precision, recall, AP, and NDCG against ground-truth context IDs; supports the packet's baseline claim that recall/hit-rate are standard, but not the whole-span split metric."},
  {system: "TruLens RAG Triad", url: "https://www.trulens.org/getting_started/core_concepts/rag_triad/", overlap: "Ships context relevance/groundedness/answer relevance checks; groundedness separates responses into claims and searches retrieved context for support, overlapping with answer-support evaluation rather than exact chunk-boundary containment."},
  {system: "vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "Serving/KV-cache/kernel stacks, not RAG retrieval evaluators; no meaningful overlap found with recall@k versus answer-completeness@k metric mechanism."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: "Partial. The L0 artifact is reproducible-looking and the split-rate mechanism is exact under its definitions, but realistic scale/workload is not established: 8 seeds x 200 synthetic docs/cell, lexical BM25 only, distinctive gold tokens force recall@k=1.000 in every cell, chunk sizes 32/64/128 are smaller than many production RAG settings, and no real QA corpus, dense retriever, semantic chunker, or downstream EM/F1 test is reported. The overlap control is strong: the effect disappears when overlap >= span_len, so the claim only holds for answer spans longer than effective overlap."
RATIONALE: "This is not a systems design contribution in the vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM sense; it is a metric-validity mechanism and small measurement artifact. The baseline is not a strawman: LlamaIndex documents hit-rate/recall among standard retriever evaluation metrics. But the obvious competitor is not absent from practice: Ragas and DeepEval ship contextual recall metrics that measure whether retrieved context supports/reference-covers answer claims, and TruLens ships groundedness/context checks. Those are not identical to deterministic whole-gold-span-in-one-chunk completeness@k, so I do not mark this red as already fully implemented. However, the systems insight is modest and the magnitude is not yet credible at realistic workload because the packet's own caveat says the synthetic lexical setup always retrieves a fragment, making the recall-completeness gap upper-bound-flavored."
